## Privilege Requirements

### With Administrator Privileges (Recommended)
- All 11 artifact sources accessible
- Complete forensic coverage
- Prefetch file analysis (`C:\Windows\Prefetch`)
- USB device tracking (`HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Enum\USBSTOR`)
- Security Event Log parsing (Process creation 4688, logons 4624/4625, audit log clear 1102)

### Without Administrator Privileges
- 9 out of 11 artifact sources accessible
- Missing: Prefetch files, USB device history, Security Event Log
- System Event Logs (Services 7045, shutdowns 1074) and PowerShell ScriptBlock (4104) still fully accessible
- TraceFinder degrades gracefully and continues collecting all available artifacts

---

## Artifact Coverage

| Category | Artifacts | Admin Required? | Forensic Value |
| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |
| **Execution** | UserAssist, Prefetch, Security 4688 | Partial | High - Shows GUI & process executions with run counts |
| **File Activity** | Recent Files (`.lnk`), RecentDocs | No | High - Documents and shortcuts opened |
| **Network** | Chrome, Edge, Brave, Opera, Vivaldi, Firefox (All profiles) | No | High - Web activity, domain lookups, and downloads |
| **Hardware** | USB Devices (`USBSTOR`) | Yes | Critical - Identifies potential data exfiltration |
| **Command Line** | PowerShell history, RunMRU, ScriptBlocks (4104) | No | Critical - Script execution tracking & commands |
| **Windows Events** | System (7045, 1074, 6005, 104), Security, PowerShell | Partial | Critical - Service installation, shutdowns, log tampering |
| **Registry** | TypedPaths | No | Medium - Manual navigation tracking in Explorer |

